<%#
  A PANEL'S OWN VIEW BUTTONS: Tiles / List for Files, and Browser too for a folder panel
  (Maker::ProjectKind.offered_views, which the door validates against, so the buttons and the door
  cannot disagree about what a panel offers). One partial for both panels since 2026-11-16; it was
  the same markup written out in projects/_folder_panel and projects/_attachments.

  BUTTONS, NOT LINKS, because this is a WRITE: the choice is persisted on the project row
  (Projects::PanelsController#update's `view` branch), not remembered in a cookie. Each posts
  `view[<key>]=<value>`.

  `aria-pressed` CARRIES THE STATE THE `active` CLASS DRAWS (2026-11-02, the UX audit's I): a screen
  reader heard plain buttons and no way to tell which view was on.

  THE SWITCH HAPPENS IN PLACE (2026-11-16, at the owner's report). `in_place` asks the door to
  redirect to the page NAMING THIS PANEL, and ProjectsController#show answers Turbo with a stream
  that replaces this panel (a folder panel's frame, the Files panel's section) and nothing else. Without it the door redirects to the page,
  which redraws every panel, sends every browser on it back to its top folder and moves the window.
  With no JavaScript the same form still lands on the page, at the panel's anchor.

  THE OPEN FOLDERS RIDE ALONG (2026-11-24, click-through panels): each button posts `at`, every
  panel's open folder as this render has it (@panel_at), and the door carries it into the redirect,
  so switching Tiles to List keeps the panel in the folder it was in — and every other panel in
  its own. Nothing when no folder is open. AT THE PRESS the form takes them from the page's URL
  instead (panel_at_controller.js#carry): a folder opened in another panel since this render redrew
  only that panel, so the inputs drawn here no longer know it. They stay for a browser with no
  JavaScript, stale at most.

  NOT IN THE EDITOR. Its slots carry a DRAFT view beside the panel, and a stream that replaced the
  panel under it would leave the two disagreeing. There a press keeps the answer it always had.

  `autofocus` IS SET ONLY IN THE ANSWER TO A PRESS (@switched_panel, set by that stream render): the
  button that was pressed is replaced with the rest of its section, and Turbo hands the focus to the
  marked one once the stream is in. A page load must mark none, or every visit would pull the
  keyboard and the window to a view button (project_panels_test.rb pins both).

  Locals: key (the panel's layout key), view (its current view), label (the group's accessible name).
%>
<div class="view-toggle" role="group" aria-label="<%= label %>">
  <% Maker::ProjectKind.offered_views(key).each do |value| %>
    <% on = view == value %>
    <%= button_to value.capitalize, project_panels_path(@project), method: :patch,
                  params: { view: { key => value }, in_place: ("1" unless @editing), at: @panel_at.presence }.compact,
                  form: (@editing ? {} : { data: { action: "submit->panel-at#carry" } }),
                  class: "toggle#{' active' if on}", "aria-pressed": on.to_s,
                  autofocus: (on && @switched_panel == key) %>
  <% end %>
</div>
